WEBVTT

00:03:22.482 --> 00:03:30.135
If we try 861 times 1001, we get 861,861,

00:03:30.135 --> 00:03:33.605
and we see something similar 
with other examples.

00:03:33.605 --> 00:03:35.405
It’s a peculiar pattern.

00:03:35.405 --> 00:03:39.577
Why would multiplying a three-digit 
number by 1001

00:03:39.577 --> 00:03:42.197
end up giving you two copies 
of that number,

00:03:42.197 --> 00:03:43.917
written one after the other?

00:03:43.917 --> 00:03:47.627
Breaking down the multiplication 
problem can give us the answer.

00:03:47.627 --> 00:03:53.594
1001 times any number x is equal 
to 1000x + x.

00:03:53.594 --> 00:04:03.104
For example, 725 times 1000 is 725,000, 
and 725 x 1 is 725.